# Trivy vulnerability ignore list
# Format: CVE-ID [expiry-date] [comment]
#
# Each entry is reviewed and justified below.

# CVE-2026-47429 — vitest UI server arbitrary file read
# Affected package: vitest (node_modules copied into production image)
# Justification: vitest is a test runner / devDependency. The vulnerability
# requires the Vitest UI server to be actively running (`vitest --ui`). We
# never run `vitest --ui` inside Docker containers; vitest is not invoked at
# runtime. Not exploitable in this context.
CVE-2026-47429

# CVE-2024-24790 — golang stdlib net/netip: unexpected behavior for IPv4-mapped IPv6 addresses
# Affected package: @esbuild/linux-x64 (Go binary compiled with Go <1.21.11 / <1.22.4)
# Justification: esbuild is a JavaScript/TypeScript bundler; it makes no network calls
# and does not use net/netip at runtime. Not exploitable in this context.
# Resolution: will resolve automatically when esbuild releases a binary built with Go ≥1.22.4.
CVE-2024-24790

# CVE-2025-68121 — golang stdlib crypto/tls: incorrect cert validation during TLS session resumption
# Affected package: @esbuild/linux-x64 (Go binary compiled with Go <1.24.13 / <1.25.7)
# Justification: esbuild does not perform any TLS connections; it is a build-time
# code transformation tool. Not exploitable in this context.
# Resolution: will resolve automatically when esbuild releases a binary built with Go ≥1.25.7.
CVE-2025-68121
